{"base_manifest_sha256":"531f85386978d805de3756d2d1c70d748a4cd392c0caad3c4173e8a9d9c6fa06","review":{"basis":"Artifact-defined confirmed history with explicit UTC/24x7 fixed and calendar boundaries; external conformance remains deferred.","date":"2026-10-24","decisions":["Pine v1/v2 preserve implicit historical lookahead_on, with positional x/y/z/a and gaps=false.","Pine v3/v4 use security(symbol,resolution,expression,gaps,lookahead); v5/v6 use request.security and timeframe. Default gaps/lookahead are off from v3.","Named barmerge constants are required for v5/v6 flags; v3/v4 additionally accept literal bool. Unresolved v5 calc_bars_count defaults are not used.","Unconditional global requests use literal qualified symbol/timeframe. Numeric/bool scalar or flat mixed numeric/bool tuples are computed from bounded pure typed expressions and transitive immutable global bar declarations, frozen inputs, scalar UDFs with private locals/state, conditional values and expression history with literal offsets. Each selected declaration runs once per requested bar in source order. Captured globals with writes or var persistence, collections, loops, strings, nested/dynamic/local requests and trading/output effects are excluded. Max 16 result components, 128 closure nodes, 16 levels; numeric scalar int promotion retains the previous ABI.","Missing numeric values and bool values before v6 are na; missing bool components are false in v6, including gaps_on and before the first visible bar. Tuple components share one availability event. Every requested expression uses the existing typed runtime and the complete frozen input schema/settings; its state belongs to the requested context. No formula is evaluated on the primary bars on behalf of a request. Physical close history for TR/ATR is read in that same requested context.","Aligned minute bars or explicit UTC D/W/M calendars. Weeks open Monday and months use actual calendar lengths. No implicit fetch, resampling or exchange selection. Missing bars remain missing.","Fixed requests preserve exact same/higher multiples. Calendar requests use availability at actual close/open boundaries, including weeks spanning a month boundary; higher calendar rank is D then W then M. Minute primaries must divide a UTC day.","Off makes a requested bar available at its close before the coincident primary close; on intentionally exposes its final historical value at its open before the coincident primary open.","Each written expression has independent state updated on requested bars; gaps_on emits only when a new availability event occurred since the previous primary observation. This gap/event mapping is an explicit artifact-defined model pending external conformance."],"external_pine_execution":false,"sources":["https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/v3/essential/context-switching-the-security-function/","https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/concepts/other-timeframes-and-data/"],"test_refs":["tests/test_contexts.py","tests/test_calendar.py","tests/test_request_expressions.py","conformance/contexts/cases.json"]},"schema_version":"openpine.request-spec.1","version_review_manifest_sha256":"019cb2a538398fce686c2475860106997959c32095001bb068b4b2c0158b8aca","versions":{"1":{"evidence":[{"entry_id":"wiki:v1:functions:security","source_record_sha256":"61dc7b5d0905fc6b57778e3ab2486d8ffcf1e005cef618723a1f215fed425deb"}],"policy":{"alignment":"utc_fixed_multiples_or_calendar_close_boundaries","availability_off":"requested_close_lte_primary_close","availability_on":"requested_open_lte_primary_open","captures":"transitive_unconditional_global_bar_declarations_without_writes","contexts":"explicit_snapshots","expression":"primitive_scalar_or_flat_tuple_with_immutable_dependency_graph_and_pure_udf","expression_history":"context_local_scalar_expression_literal_offset","flags":"bool","functions":"existing_typed_scalar_udf_with_private_locals_and_state","gaps_default":"off","gaps_off":"carry_last_available_including_n